\name{cellucid_view_rename}
\alias{cellucid_view_rename}
\title{Name a view}
\usage{
cellucid_view_rename(viewer, view, name)
}
\arguments{
\item{viewer}{A viewer \code{\link{cellucid_view}()} or \code{\link{cellucid_serve}()} returned.}
\item{view}{A view: "View N" as the Compare views list numbers its rows (the live view is View 1 while it is shown, the kept views follow in the order they were kept). Text. Required.}
\item{name}{The new name, or null for none. Either text (at least 1 character) (A name for the view, one line of text ("Early", "Day 7, treated"): its row and its pane show it beside its number ("2 \ifelse{latex}{<U+00B7>}{·} Early"), a figure's panel after its letter ("B. Early": the figure letters its panels A, B, \ldots in order, so a name needs no letter of its own). Not "View N"); or \code{NULL} (No name: the view is known by its number alone). Required.}
}
\value{
A \code{cellucid_action_request}, at once and invisibly: the action is sent now, or when the viewer's channel opens.
\code{\link{cellucid_action_result}(request)} returns its outcome (what it did, as names, counts and ids), or \code{NULL} when it had nothing to report; \code{request$step} is the history step it made.
}
\description{
Give a view a name of its own, or take it away (null): its row and its pane show it beside its number, a figure's panel title after the panel's letter ("B. Early"). The view is still named "View N" in actions.
}
\details{
The viewer's action \code{view.rename} (Views). It changes what the viewer shows: one step of the viewer's history, labeled as R's, undone like any other. The state it can change: \code{views}.
}
\seealso{
\code{\link{cellucid_act}()} sends any action by its type, and \code{\link{cellucid_action_result}()}
collects its answer.
}
\examples{
if (interactive() && requireNamespace("SeuratObject", quietly = TRUE)) {
  data("pbmc_small", package = "SeuratObject")
  viewer <- cellucid_view(SeuratObject::UpdateSeuratObject(pbmc_small))
  request <- cellucid_view_rename(viewer, name = "Early",
      view = "View 1")
  print(request)
  # cellucid_action_result(request) waits for its outcome.
  cellucid_stop(viewer)
}
}
